ty Order)\n    41→\n    42→### CRITICAL\n    43→1. **False character merge: \"the mummer\" merged with \"Prince Prospero\"**\n    44→   - Problem: \"the mummer\" is listed as an alias of Prince Prospero, but it refers to the Red Death personification\n    45→   - Evidence from text:\n    46→     - \"But the mummer had gone so far as to assume the type of the Red Death. His vesture was dabbled in blood\"\n    47→     - \"seizing the mummer, whose tall figure stood erect and motionless within the shadow of the ebony clock\"\n    48→   - Impact: The main antagonist is incorrectly merged with the protagonist (-2 point character score)\n    49→   - Root cause: The fix in attempt 2 may have made epithet merging too aggressive\n    50→   - Location: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` - alias resolution logic\n    51→   - Fix approach: Need context-aware epithet matching - \"the mummer\" clearly refers to a different entity (the intruder/stranger) not the prince\n    52→\n    53→2. **Missing character: The Red Death / Masked Figure**\n    54→   - Problem: The antagonist of the story is not present as a character entry\n    55→   - Evidence: Multiple text references to this entity:\n    56→     - \"the stranger\"\n    57→     - \"the figure\"\n    58→     - \"the masked figure\"\n    59→     - \"the intruder\"\n    60→     - \"the mummer\" (currently mis-merged with Prospero)\n    61→   - Impact: Major character missing\n    62→   - Location: Character extraction pipeline\n    63→   - Fix approach: After fixing issue #1, this character should emerge naturally\n    64→\n    65→### HIGH\n    66→3. **Mention count still low for Prince Prospero**\n    67→   - Problem: Character shows 6 mentions, but pronunciation shows 18 \"Prospero\" + 9 \"Prince\" occurrences\n    68→   - Evidence: Clear discrepancy between pronunciation counting and character counting\n    69→   - Location: Mention count aggregation in character pipeline\n    70→   - Fix: Ensure mention counts a